CSS variables & theming Guide Every color, space, radius, and font in vd3 is a CSS custom property (--vd-*). Override them in your own stylesheet and the whole system updates — no recompile, no JavaScript. This token layer ships with @vanduo-oss/vd3. Global overrides Scoped overridesCustom properties cascade, so you can re-theme one subtree: The three token tiersTierExamplesPalette--vd-blue-6, --vd-gray-0…9 — active scales (Open Color by default; --vd-oc-*/--vd-fib-* are the raw palette sources)Semantic--vd-color-primary, --vd-bg-primary, --vd-text-primary, --vd-border-colorComponent--vd-btn-border-radius, --vd-card-bg — per-component knobs Semantic tokens reference palette tokens; component tokens reference semantic ones. Override at the tier that matches your intent. Dark mode is the same mechanism You rarely write this by hand — useThemePreference().setTheme('dark') or the theme customizer flips data-theme and the stylesheet remaps the tokens. Bridge an app-owned toggle Vue 3 Already have a light/dark toggle (e.g. @nuxtjs/color-mode, a Pinia store, or your own ref)? The useThemeBridge composable from @vanduo-oss/vd3 keeps vd3 in sync with it instead of adding a second source of truth. Pass a Ref<'light' | 'dark' | 'system'>. The bridge re-syncs on mount and whenever the ref changes — useful for SSR / Nuxt apps where the host framework owns color mode. Theming in actionColor palette CoreEvery palette and semantic token you can override.Theme switcher ComponentDrop-in light / dark / system toggle.Theme customizer ComponentLive-edit tokens and preview the result instantly.
Tier | Examples
Palette | --vd-blue-6, --vd-gray-0…9 — active scales (Open Color by default; --vd-oc-*/--vd-fib-* are the raw palette sources)
Semantic | --vd-color-primary, --vd-bg-primary, --vd-text-primary, --vd-border-color
Component | --vd-btn-border-radius, --vd-card-bg — per-component knobs
/* Override tokens in your own stylesheet — cascades everywhere */
:root {
  --vd-color-primary: #6366f1;
  --vd-color-primary-dark: #4f46e5;
  --vd-radius-fib-5: 0.5rem;
  --vd-font-family-base: 'Inter', sans-serif;
}
/* Scope overrides to a subtree — e.g. a "danger zone" panel */
.danger-zone {
  --vd-color-primary: var(--vd-color-danger);
}
/* Flipping data-theme (or useThemePreference().setTheme) is enough.
   The stylesheet already remaps --vd-bg-primary, --vd-text-primary, and
   related tokens. Hex overrides below are optional brand tweaks. */
[data-theme="dark"] {
  --vd-color-primary: #6366f1; /* optional brand override */
}
import { computed } from 'vue';
import { useThemeBridge } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3';
import { useColorMode } from '@nuxtjs/color-mode'; // any owner of light/dark

// vd3 keys dark mode off [data-theme] on <html>. When another system owns
// the toggle, hand it that system's mode ref and vd3 follows along:
const colorMode = useColorMode();
useThemeBridge(computed(() => colorMode.preference));

// On mount and on every change, the bridge sets [data-theme] AND re-derives
// the default accent for the active scheme — no duplicate toggle UI needed.

