Installation & Integration Guide Reference for installing @vanduo-oss/vd3: plugin options, the optional canvas bundle, vite-ssg, and Nuxt. For a five-minute first page, start at Getting started. vd3 is Vue 3 only. What tree-shakes. Named JS imports tree-shake. VanduoVue does not register components globally — import each Vd* you use. @vanduo-oss/vd3/css is the full stylesheet; /css/core is the same tree without bundled icon fonts, not a tokens-only sheet. Install the package Install the design system. Add charts or flowchart if your app needs them. Register the plugin & styles Import @vanduo-oss/vd3/css once in your entry file so the whole stylesheet is loaded, then install the plugin: VanduoVue only applies theme defaults and the storage prefix — it does not register components globally: OptionTypeDescriptionthemeDefaultsPartial<ThemeDefaults>Site-specific overrides shallow-merged over the generated theme baseline (e.g. { PRIMARY_DARK: 'green' }). Applied synchronously on install, before the theme model first reads its defaults. Optional.storagePrefixstringlocalStorage key prefix for theme preferences (default "vanduo-"). Applied synchronously on install, before the first storage read. Use a unique prefix when two apps share an origin so keys do not collide. Example: "my-app-" → my-app-theme-preference, my-app-palette, … Use the components Import Vd* components from @vanduo-oss/vd3 — typed, tree-shakeable, ready to compose: Import each optional package and its stylesheet: vite-ssg & SSR Every Vd* component is SSR-safe — no window or DOM access at module or setup scope, with browser-only work (observers, listeners) deferred to onMounted. Register the plugin inside the vite-ssg setup callback: Import @vanduo-oss/vd3/css in the entry so the stylesheet is baked into the prerendered HTML (no flash of unstyled content). Set themeDefaults (and storagePrefix if you need it) in the setup callback so the first server-rendered paint matches the client. Nuxt Load the stylesheet from nuxt.config, then install VanduoVue in a client plugin so localStorage theming stays off the server: If @nuxtjs/color-mode already owns light/dark, bridge it instead of adding a second toggle: More on the bridge: CSS variables & theming. Next stepsGetting started GuideScaffold a Vue app and add vd3 in a few minutes.vd3 Architecture GuideTokens to CSS to components — how the package is built.Browse components ComponentStart with Button and explore the reference.
Option | Type | Description
themeDefaults | Partial<ThemeDefaults> | Site-specific overrides shallow-merged over the generated theme baseline (e.g. { PRIMARY_DARK: 'green' }). Applied synchronously on install, before the theme model first reads its defaults. Optional.
storagePrefix | string | localStorage key prefix for theme preferences (default "vanduo-"). Applied synchronously on install, before the first storage read. Use a unique prefix when two apps share an origin so keys do not collide. Example: "my-app-" → my-app-theme-preference, my-app-palette, …
# The Vue 3 component library (tokens + CSS + components)
pnpm add @vanduo-oss/vd3

# Charts and flowchart ship as dedicated packages
pnpm add @vanduo-oss/vd3-charts
pnpm add @vanduo-oss/vd3-flowchart
// main.ts — register the plugin and the stylesheet once
import { createApp } from 'vue';
import { VanduoVue } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3';
import '@vanduo-oss/vd3/css';
import App from './App.vue';

createApp(App).use(VanduoVue).mount('#app');
// Plugin options apply synchronously on install, before the first storage read.
app.use(VanduoVue, {
  storagePrefix: 'my-app-',           // default 'vanduo-'
  themeDefaults: { PRIMARY_DARK: 'green' },
});
<script setup lang="ts">
import { VdCard, VdButton } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3';
</script>

<template>
  <VdCard>
    <h1>Build fast with vd3</h1>
    <p class="vd-text-lg vd-text-muted">First-class Vue 3 components.</p>
    <VdButton variant="primary" size="lg">Get started</VdButton>
  </VdCard>
</template>
// Optional charts and flowchart packages.
import { VdChart } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3-charts';
import '@vanduo-oss/vd3-charts/css';

import { VdFlowchart } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3-flowchart';
import '@vanduo-oss/vd3-flowchart/css';
// main.ts — SSR / SSG entry with vite-ssg
import { ViteSSG } from 'vite-ssg';
import { VanduoVue } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3';
import '@vanduo-oss/vd3/css';
import App from './App.vue';
import { routes } from './routes';

export const createApp = ViteSSG(App, { routes }, ({ app }) => {
  app.use(VanduoVue, {
    storagePrefix: 'my-app-',
    themeDefaults: { PRIMARY_DARK: 'green' },
  });
});

