vd3 Architecture Guide vd3 combines design tokens, CSS, and typed Vue components. Import the components you use and one stylesheet. The layers below explain how they fit together. 1 Design tokens (DTCG)DTCG JSON defines color scales and theme metadata.2 Generated color CSSThe token build generates color variables and tokens.json for tooling.3 Component CSSAuthored layout, component, utility, and effect styles share the generated colors.4 Vue components & composablesTyped Vue components and composables use the shared styles and manage their own listeners. What you import Start with named component imports and either the full or icon-free stylesheet. Entry pointWhat it is@vanduo-oss/vd3Named components, composables, the optional configuration plugin, and types.@vanduo-oss/vd3/cssFull CSS, including icons. Import once.@vanduo-oss/vd3/css/coreFull CSS without bundled icons. Supply your own icons.@vanduo-oss/vd3/tokens.jsonFlat { "--vd-name": value } map for tooling. How the package is built Maintainers run this pipeline. Applications install its prebuilt output. Wiring an appVanduoVue sets optional theme defaults. Import each component where you use it; the plugin does not register components. Lifecycle and shared state Components attach listeners on mount and clean them up on unmount. Theme preferences and toast queues use module-wide state. A storage prefix changes persistence keys; it does not isolate apps. Avoid writing request-specific theme or toast state during SSR. Next stepsInstallation & Integration GuideInstall, choose CSS, and import components.vd3 ecosystem GuideHow the design system, charts, flowchart, and docs fit together.CSS variables & theming GuideOverride the generated token layer for your brand.
Entry point | What it is
@vanduo-oss/vd3 | Named components, composables, the optional configuration plugin, and types.
@vanduo-oss/vd3/css | Full CSS, including icons. Import once.
@vanduo-oss/vd3/css/core | Full CSS without bundled icons. Supply your own icons.
@vanduo-oss/vd3/tokens.json | Flat { "--vd-name": value } map for tooling.
# How the package is built (you consume the prebuilt dist/)
clean-dist         # wipe dist/
build-tokens.mjs   # DTCG JSON  ->  generated color CSS + tokens.json
build-css.mjs      # inline every layer  ->  vd3.min.css (+ core, icon-free)
vite build         # SFCs  ->  ESM/CJS barrel
vue-tsc            # emit .d.ts types
check-class-coverage.mjs   # verify every documented class ships
// main.ts — optional theme defaults; import components in your .vue files
import { createApp } from 'vue';
import { VanduoVue } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3';
import '@vanduo-oss/vd3/css';          // choose one stylesheet
import App from './App.vue';

createApp(App).use(VanduoVue).mount('#app');
// Theme and toast state is currently shared within the loaded module.
import { VdToastContainer, useToast, useThemePreference } from '@vanduo-oss/vd3';

// Mount <VdToastContainer /> once (e.g. in App.vue) so toasts have somewhere to go.
const toast = useToast();
toast.success('Saved');

const theme = useThemePreference();
theme.setTheme('dark');

